@* What an anonymous visitor meets at an [Authorize] route: a bounce to the identity provider
   with the address they were heading for kept, so signing in lands them where they meant to go
   rather than on the dashboard.

   Rendered by the router's NotAuthorized branch (see Routes) — inside the layout, which is why
   AppShell's own AuthorizeView has a signed-out arm at all.

   forceLoad because /login is an endpoint, not a Blazor route: it hands the request to the OIDC
   challenge, which has to leave the circuit behind. *@

@inject NavigationManager Nav

@code {
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        var current = new Uri(Nav.Uri).PathAndQuery;
        Nav.NavigateTo(AppRoutes.LoginReturningTo(current), forceLoad: true);
    }
}
